{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mass.TauQuantumIntegerForm","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mass.TauQuantumIntegerForm","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Matrix.Determinant.Basic"],"declarations":3,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.TauQuantumInteger.tau_bar_even","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.TauQuantumInteger.tau_bar_even","kind":"theorem","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/TauQuantumIntegerForm.lean#L70-L93","doc":"**τ is bar-even: `τ(q⁻¹) = τ(q)`** (invariant under the Hecke bar-involution `q ↦ q⁻¹`), over any\nfield `K` with `q, q+1, 2` invertible. Immediate consequence of the `[2]_q` form. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.TauQuantumInteger.tau_quantum_integer_form","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.TauQuantumInteger.tau_quantum_integer_form","kind":"theorem","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/TauQuantumIntegerForm.lean#L47-L68","doc":"**τ is a rational function of the quantum integer `[2]_q = q + q⁻¹` alone:**\n`τ(q) = 3(3[2]² + 2)/(4([2]+2))`. Stated over **any field `K`** with `q, q+1, 2` invertible (e.g.\n`K = ℚ(q)`, the Hecke fraction field) — *not* `ℝ`. The proved closed form `3(3q⁴+8q²+3)/(4q(q+1)²)`\ncollapses onto `[2]_q`, the Hecke / q-difference fingerprint. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.TauQuantumInteger.transfer_det_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.TauQuantumInteger.transfer_det_one","kind":"theorem","line":40,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/TauQuantumIntegerForm.lean#L40-L45","doc":"**`M ∈ SL₂(R)` over ANY commutative ring** — the depth-2 transfer matrix `!![τ,-1;1,0]` has\n`det = 1` (so eigenvalues multiply to 1, sum to the trace). Trace-agnostic and ring-universal: no\nordering and no division are used, so this is *not* an `ℝ`-statement. ","signatureChunk":0}]}